  "narrative": {
    "text": "UML class diagram of the Supply Chain profile, reproduced small: class names are mostly legible but most attribute text is not, so names are given as drawn and approximately. Three parents sit above the frame: Core/ Action, Core/ Artifact and Core/ DefinedProcess. The left column hangs action classes from Core/Action: CreateAction with HarvestingAction (or similar), AssemblyAction, ManufactureAction and ReproduceAction beneath it; UseAction with BoundaryCrossingAction, InspectionAction, OutOfSpecAction, PlanAction, ResolutionAction, a state-related action and TestAction; ModifyAction with ChangeAction, StorageAction and TransportAction; then BoundaryDefinitionAction, DestroyAction and ResponsibilityChangeAction. The right column mirrors it with process classes from Core/DefinedProcess: CreateProcess with InstantiateVirtualHardwareProcess, HarvestProcess, AssemblyProcess, ManufactureProcess and ReproduceProcess; UseProcess with InspectionProcess, PlanProcess, DefinedStateProcess and TestProcess among others; ModifyProcess with ChangeProcess, StorageProcess and TransportProcess; then BoundaryDefinitionProcess, DestroyProcess and ResponsibilityChangeProcess. A single class near the top centre hangs from Core/Artifact. Many classes carry one or more attribute rows shaded red, and a small 'Enumerations' frame at the lower right holds one enumeration.",
